// ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// SCHEDULE OF AUTHORITY (SOA) — MAP EPC ONLY
//
// Governs two things, both scoped to MAP's EPC approval flow:
//   1. Which designation(s) may propose/check/approve an EPC whose
//      Tata Hitachi share (EPF.tataHitachiPoAmount — dealer share
//      excluded) falls in a given amount band.
//   2. The auto-approval bypass: if the EPC creator's designation is
//      APPROVER-eligible for the matched band, the EPC is approved
//      directly and no WorkflowInstance is created at all.
//
// Deliberately kept OUT of the Designation table and out of the
// existing WorkflowTemplate/TemplateStage/TemplateApprover system —
// this is MAP-specific policy, not an org-wide identity concern, and
// not the same mechanism as the existing budget-banded template
// routing (which stays keyed on EPF.eventBudget via budgetMap/
// templateMatchResolvers and is untouched by this table).
//
// CHECKER is defined but not yet consumed by any bypass logic — the
// current requirement only bypasses on APPROVER eligibility. Kept in
// the enum so the admin screen can record Checker assignments now
// without a future schema change when Checker-stage logic is added.
//
// Inheritance rule (service-layer, not enforced here): APPROVER
// eligibility inherits upward — a designation listed as Approver on a
// higher tier is also eligible for every lower tier's amount. PROPOSER
// and CHECKER are strict-match only, no inheritance.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

enum AuthorityRole {
  PROPOSER
  CHECKER
  APPROVER
}

enum NotificationType {
  APPROVAL_PENDING   // a workflow stage now requires this user's approval
  APPROVAL_DECISION  // an approval/rejection/clarify happened on something this user owns
  REPORT_STATUS      // event report validated/rejected/clarification requested
  GENERIC            // catch-all for future apps that don't fit the above
}

